    "result": "Perfect! The fix has been successfully applied and compiled. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Problem:** The `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly did work.\n\n**Root Cause:** In the `frai` CLI, when delegating to the `frai-gate` subcommand, the code was relying on commander.js's parsed `args` parameter. However, commander was consuming the `--ci` global option before the gate handler received it, so it never got passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**Solution:** Modified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Extract all original arguments from `process.argv` after the 'gate' command\n2. Pass those raw arguments directly to the `frai-gate` CLI, bypassing commander's option parsing\n\nThis ensures flags like `--ci` are passed through correctly to the delegated command.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Modified the gate command handler to use `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)` instead of relying on commander's parsed `args`\n- Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Verified the fix works: `frai gate init --ci` now successfully creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
